outcome:
Three things the duration report's docs claim are tested only on synthetic artifacts:
- the real Node runner emits per-file test:summary events with `file` set under process isolation (real-run tests assert test entries but never files);
- Vitest 4 accepts `--reporter=default --reporter=json --outputFile.json=...` and writes the testResults / startTime / endTime / assertionResults shape;
- Vitest's per-test duration includes per-test hooks (confirmed in source; only the Node hook inclusion has a real-runner test).
A regression in any of them silently empties the slow-file list or turns the report unreadable. The fix adds a real-run assertion that a Node fixture yields a per-file entry under a zero file budget. It pins the Vitest JSON shape with a minimal real Vitest invocation where the suite can run Vitest, or documents the reliance. Optionally it drops the `m` flag from the Vitest timeout regex, per the reviewer's Note.
